--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Difference between the two uml designs:

    The before uml has one class that we didn't think we need at the beginning and one class we thought we
needed and at the end we got rid of.
The Difference is that the before uml design has a Stem class and does not have the numericEnergyCounter class
where the after uml design does not have a stem class and has numericEnergyCounter class.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Open world:

    There are two things that had to be dealt with in an open world, (1)) terrain (2) trees, we implemented
them differently.
(1) Terrain: the terrain implemented in a way where there are no blocks outside of the frame we see as a
             a player, and as the avatar walks left or right the terrain is being built in run time and the
             blocks that gets outside of the frame gets removed from teh game objects.
             using a hash function insures us when we build the terrain back again it will be the same shape.
             for example if the avatar moves right then every ground block on the left side that got outside
             of the frame gets removed and every empty spaces on the right that hes gonna reach gets build
             instantly with new blocks
(2) Trees:  on the other hand the trees implemented in a way that they exists from the beginning and until the
            game ends and the user closes it,meaning the trees never gets deleted and recreated.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Tree Package:

    initially we thought we need 3 classes: Stem, Leaf and tree where Tree instance uses instances of Leaf and
Stem combined. After a secondary thought we found out that there is no specific and special use of a stem
instance and that it doesn't have special characteristics that makes it different which lead to creating the
stem inside the class tree and where instances of leaf also created.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Design Dilemmas:

(1).Designing the character where is the wand too outside his body borders or not, which can lead to
unexpected behaviour when coming to an empty block between two blocks.
(2).In open world the dilemma was if the trees should be deleted and recreated, but that would make issues
with deleting the leaves of the tree, for example if the tree gets deleted because the stem is already out of
frame but the leaves are still in the frame, then suddenly the leaves disappear and the player would notice,
leading to the decision that trees would always exist

